course: dictionary
lesson: 2458
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Danish can mean from Denmark, the language spoken there, or a sweet pastry. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Ask yourself: what is this sentence about?
explain: «LEGO is a Danish company founded in 1932.» A company comes from a country, so Danish means from Denmark. In «its name comes from the Danish «leg godt»», Danish describes words, so it means the language.
explain: «The Baltic Sea... its only exit is through narrow Danish straits.» Straits are a kind of water, so Danish here means from or belonging to Denmark. A breakfast pastry would not fit, so that meaning is wrong.
explain: Always test your meaning. Put it into the sentence in place of the word. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: Danish means from Denmark, or to do with Denmark and its people.
fact: Danish is also the language spoken in Denmark.
fact: A danish, or Danish pastry, is a sweet, flaky pastry, often with fruit, custard or icing.
fact: Denmark is a country in northern Europe.
fact: LEGO is a Danish company, and its name comes from the Danish words «leg godt», meaning «play well».
exercise: «LEGO is a Danish company founded in 1932.» What does Danish mean here? | Made of wood | Spoken in Sydney | A sweet, flaky pastry | *From Denmark
exercise: «...its name comes from the Danish «leg godt», meaning «play well».» Here Danish means: | The people of Sydney | A large lake | *The language of Denmark | A pastry with custard
exercise: What is a danish, the breakfast treat you can buy in bakeries and cafés? | A kind of Viking ship | A company that makes toys | A narrow sea channel | *A sweet, flaky pastry, often with fruit or custard
test:
«The Sydney Opera House, designed by the Danish architect Jørn Utzon, opened in 1973.» Here Danish means: | *From Denmark | The language of Denmark | A sweet pastry | Very old
test:
«The Baltic Sea is brackish... its only exit is through narrow Danish straits.» Danish here means: | The language spoken in Sweden | *From or belonging to Denmark | A sweet, flaky pastry | Very salty
exam: Which meaning of danish fits in a sentence about ordering one with your coffee in a café? | A type of Viking ship | The language of Denmark | *A sweet, flaky pastry | From Denmark
